---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="hideouts.io collects nothing: no cookies, no analytics, no trackers, no third-party requests."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="This site collects nothing."
    lead="No cookies, no analytics, no trackers, no fingerprinting, no third-party requests. That’s the whole policy; the rest of this page explains how it’s enforced."
  />
  <div class="container-x pt-12">
    <div class="prose-readme max-w-[46rem]">
      <h2>What happens when you visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No cookies</strong> are set, so there’s no consent banner.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No analytics or tracking scripts</strong> of any kind, first- or third-party.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No third-party requests.</strong> Fonts, images, diagrams, and scripts are all served from
          hideouts.io. README images are copied here at build time so your browser never contacts GitHub or an image CDN
          while you read.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Search runs in your browser.</strong> The search index is a static file; what you type is never sent
          anywhere.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Theme choice</strong> (light or dark) is stored in your browser’s local storage only if you use the
          toggle. It never leaves your device.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it’s enforced</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A strict <strong>Content Security Policy</strong> only allows scripts, styles, images, and connections from
          this origin, and scripts only by hash.
        </li>
        <li>
          <code>Referrer-Policy: no-referrer</code> means sites you follow a link to aren’t told you came from here.
        </li>
        <li>Every build fails if a page references anything outside the published project list.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The hosting provider</h2>
      <p>
        The site is static files served by GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub processes your IP address to deliver
        the page and may keep standard server logs under
        <a
          href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          GitHub’s privacy statement
        </a>
        . hideouts doesn’t receive or look at those logs.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to GitHub</h2>
      <p>Download and source links go to GitHub. Once you follow one, GitHub’s own privacy practices apply.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
